# UI Component Library Style Guide v4.2.1 (Excerpt)
## Section 3.4: Enumerated Types and State Machines

### Rule 3.4.1 (Addition)
Adding a new value to an existing enumeration is considered a MINOR change, NOT a BREAKING change, PROVIDED THAT all consumer implementations are required to handle unknown values gracefully (e.g., via a default case or fallback rendering).

### Rule 3.4.2 (Strict Mode Exception)
If an enumeration is annotated with `@StrictConsumers`, the library guarantees that consumers will ONLY receive defined values. In this specific context, adding a new value is a MAJOR (Breaking) change because existing consumers lacking the new case in their switch statements will encounter runtime errors or unhandled exception crashes.

### Rule 3.4.3 (Deprecation)
Marking a value as `@Deprecated` is non-breaking. Removing it is breaking.

