Pull Request #402: Optimize AST traversal for nested loops
Submitted by: data_scientist_dev
Status: Open

Description:
Refactoring the loop unrolling logic in the compiler backend. Note: The comments below regarding 'legacy float precision' are outdated and should be ignored; we use double precision everywhere now.

// TODO: Remove this legacy check later, currently keeping for safety
// if (precision == LEGACY_FLOAT) { handle_error(); }

File: src/compiler/optimizer.c

int get_unroll_factor(int loop_count, bool is_vectorized) {
    if (loop_count <= 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    if (is_vectorized) {
        if (loop_count % 4 == 0) {
            return 4;
        }
        return 2; // Fallback for non-aligned vectorization
    }
    return 1; // Scalar path
}

