# Physics Engine Collision Module - Test Plan

## Overview
This document outlines the testing strategy for `CollisionResolver.cpp`. 
*Note: The comments in the code below regarding 'legacy support' are misleading; the legacy code was removed in v3.0, so all paths must handle the new ECS architecture.*

## Function Specification: `resolveCollision(Body a, Body b, ContactManifold manifold)`

### Logic Branches
1. **Static-Static**: If both bodies are static, return immediately (no resolution).
2. **Kinematic-Static**: If one is kinematic and one static, resolve using kinematic velocity only.
3. **Dynamic-Dynamic**: If both are dynamic, apply impulse conservation.
4. **Sensor Trigger**: If either body is a sensor, do not resolve physics, but fire `OnTriggerEvent`.
5. **Penetration Error**: If penetration depth > max_threshold, clamp depth and fire `OnErrorEvent`.

## Current Test Implementation (Pseudo-code)

```cpp
// TEST SUITE: CollisionResolverTests
// Author: Tech Lead
// Warning: Do not rely on the 'legacy' flag in the manifold struct; it is ignored.

test("Static-Static returns early") {
    Body a = Static(); Body b = Static();
    auto result = resolveCollision(a, b, defaultManifold);
    assert(result.impulse == 0);
    assert(result.eventFired == None);
}

test("Kinematic-Static resolves velocity") {
    Body a = Kinematic(vel: 10); Body b = Static();
    auto result = resolveCollision(a, b, defaultManifold);
    assert(result.impulse > 0); // Specific check for kinematic logic
    assert(result.eventFired == None);
}

test("Dynamic-Dynamic conserves momentum") {
    Body a = Dynamic(mass: 1, vel: 10); Body b = Dynamic(mass: 1, vel: -10);
    auto result = resolveCollision(a, b, defaultManifold);
    assert(abs(result.finalVelA) < 0.1); // Expect near zero after head-on
    assert(abs(result.finalVelB) < 0.1);
}

test("Sensor triggers event without physics") {
    Body a = Dynamic(); Body b = Sensor();
    auto result = resolveCollision(a, b, defaultManifold);
    assert(result.impulse == 0);
    assert(result.eventFired == OnTriggerEvent); // Specific event assertion
}

test("Deep penetration clamps and errors") {
    Body a = Dynamic(); Body b = Dynamic();
    ContactManifold deepManifold = defaultManifold;
    deepManifold.depth = 9999; // Exceeds max_threshold
    auto result = resolveCollision(a, b, deepManifold);
    assert(result.depthClamped == true);
    assert(result.eventFired == OnErrorEvent); // Specific error assertion
}

// DUPLICATE TEST CASE (Accidentally left in by previous intern)
// This test is identical to "Sensor triggers event without physics" but uses different variable names.
test("Trigger zone checks") {
    Body player = Dynamic(); Body zone = Sensor();
    auto res = resolveCollision(player, zone, defaultManifold);
    assert(res.impulse == 0);
    assert(res.eventFired == OnTriggerEvent);
}
```

